A release dir bundles everything that rides with one OTA update, kept separate
from the build. The dir name is ARBITRARY (e.g. launch, hotfix-wifi) — the
version lives in config.env, not the dir name. Mirrors configs/<release>/.

releases/<release>/config.env  - SHAREFRAME_VERSION (X.Y.Z) + SHAREFRAME_CRITICALITY
                              (Critical|Important|Minor|Patch). Single source of
                              the version: build reads it, release reads it.
releases/<release>/notes.md    - release notes for release.json (dashboard). Optional.
releases/<release>/pre.sh      - install-check hook: runs in the OLD system before
                              any slot is written; non-zero exit aborts install.
                              Optional.
releases/<release>/post.sh     - boot-slot post-install hook: runs in the OLD system
                              after slots are written, before reboot.
                              ${mnt}=boot FAT, ${bn}=target slot. Optional.

Workflow:
  cp -r releases/example releases/<release>
  $EDITOR releases/<release>/config.env          # set version + criticality
  ./automation.sh build configs/fleet/<env> --release <release>
  ./automation.sh release prod --release <release> --from <env>-<version>

One build -> several releases: re-run `release` dev and prod (or re-cut notes)
from the same --from build; same version, no rebuild.

Run-once-with-this-update only. For run-every-update idempotent work use
overlay/usr/share/shareframe/system-migrations/ (executes in the NEW system).

Only releases/example/ is tracked; every other releases/<release>/ is gitignored.
